<title>USA: Republicans gain one U.S. Senate seat by 0221 GMT.</title>
<headline>Republicans gain one U.S. Senate seat by 0221 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Republicans had gained one U.S. Senate seat from Democrats, according to election projections of major news organisations by 9:21 p.m. EST (0221 GMT).</p>
<p>Before this election, Republicans held the majority in the U.S. Senate with 53 seats against 47 held by the Democrats.</p>
<p>Democrats needed to gain three seats to take control of the Senate because Vice President Al Gore would cast the deciding vote in the Senate in the event of a tie.</p>
<p>Of the 34 seats being decided this year, Republicans held 19 and the Democrats 15.</p>
